(104,'6788ff5f-7663-4da8-b141-1cf3022b2e9a','assistant','**How to add a new module in your existing “native‑PHP inventory” structure**\n\n| Step | What to do | Key files / folders | Tips |\n|------|------------|----------------------|------|\n| 1 | **Decide the functionality** – e.g. “Product”, “Supplier”, “Purchase Order” | — | Write a short spec (table name, fields, CRUD actions). |\n| 2 | **Create the database table** – use the same naming convention (`inventory_<module>`) | MySQL via phpMyAdmin or a migration file | Add an `id`, `added_by`, timestamps as you did with `inventory_campus`. |\n| 3 | **Add the Model** | `app/classes/models/<Module>Model.php` | Extend `Extras` just like `CampusModel` and include the table relationship. Include methods: `get<Module>Details`, `saveTransaction`, `delete<Module>`, `check<Module>Code`. |\n| 4 | **Add the Controller** | `app/classes/controllers/<Module>Controller.class.php` | Extend `<Module>Model`. Add `initSaveTransaction` / `initDelete<Module>` that call the model methods and return JSON. Use the `fileExists` helper for safety. |\n| 5 | **Add the Detail View (modal)** | `admin/<module>/details.php` | Mirror `campus_details.php`. Keep the same form structure, use `tag=\"edit-<module>\" / \"add-<module>\"`, and load via AJAX. |\n| 6 | **Add the List View (DataTable)** | `admin/<module>/index.php` | Copy `index.php`. Replace table column metadata and DataTables AJAX URL to point to `../../app/includes/get<Module>List.inc.php`. |\n| 7 | **Create the DataTable source** | `app/includes/get<Module>List.inc.php` | Return JSON in the same format the DataTables plugin expects. You can copy the logic from `getCampusList.inc.php`. |\n| 8 | **Wire up routes / links** | Update `header.layout.php` or your navigation component | Add a new link, e.g. `<a href=\"/admin/<module>/index.php\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">Manage <Module></a>` |\n| 9 | **Add any auxiliary scripts** | `public/assets/js/<module>.js` (optional) | Keep the code inside the `<script>` block of the index file or extract it into a separate file for cleaner maintenance. |\n| 10 | **Test** | Use XAMPP, open the URL, add/edit/delete records, watch audit logs | Ensure `insertAuditTrail` is called in controller actions, just like with campus. |\n\n---\n\n### Quick Code Skeleton (replace `<Module>` with your chosen name)\n\n**Model (app/classes/models/<Module>Model.php)**\n```php\n<?php\ninclude_once fileExists(\'app/classes/models/Extras.php\');\n\nclass <Module>Model extends Extras {\n    protected $conn;\n    protected $user;\n\n    public function __construct() { parent::__construct(); }\n\n    public function get<Module>Details($id=\'\') {\n        $sql = \"SELECT * FROM inventory_<module> WHERE id = \'$id\'\";\n        $data = $this->conn->query($sql);\n        return $data->num_rows > 0 ? $data->fetch_assoc() : [];\n    }\n\n    public function saveTransaction($id=\'\', $user=\'\', $code=\'\', $description=\'\') {\n        // Similar INSERT/UPDATE logic, adapt field names\n    }\n\n    public function delete<Module>($id=\'\') { /* Same DELETE pattern */ }\n\n    public function check<Module>Code($id=\'\', $code=\'\') {\n        $where = $id != \'\' ? \" AND id != \'$id\'\" : \'\';\n        $sql = \"SELECT id FROM inventory_<module> WHERE code = \'$code\' $where\";\n        $data = $this->conn->query($sql);\n        return $data->num_rows > 0;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Controller (app/classes/controllers/<Module>Controller.class.php)**\n```php\n<?php\ninclude_once fileExists(\'app/classes/Database.class.php\');\ninclude_once(fileExists(\'app/classes/models/<Module>Model.php\'));\n\nclass <Module>Controller extends <Module>Model {\n    public function initSaveTransaction($post,$files){ /* similar to CampusController */ }\n    public function initDelete<Module>($post,$files){ /* similar to CampusController */ }\n}\n\nif(isset($_GET[\'action\'])) {\n    $action = $_GET[\'action\'];\n    $mod = new <Module>Controller();\n    if($action == \'saveTransaction\') echo $mod->initSaveTransaction($_POST,$_FILES);\n    if($action == \'delete<Module>\') echo $mod->initDelete<Module>($_POST,$_FILES);\n}\n```\n\n**Details View (admin/<module>/details.php)**\n```php\n<?php\nsession_start(); // etc., just copy campus_details.php but adapt field names\n?>\n<form id=\"<module>-form\" enctype=\"multipart/form-data\">\n    <!-- hidden id, code, description, etc. -->\n</form>\n<script>\n  $(function(){\n    $(\'#<module>-form\').on(\'submit\', async function(e){\n      e.preventDefault();\n      // opsConfirm and AJAX POST to controller\n    });\n  });\n</script>\n```\n\n**List View (admin/<module>/index.php)**  \nCopy the campus index and adjust the DataTable AJAX URL, column names, and button tags.\n\n---\n\n### Next Steps\n\n1. **Tell me which module you’d like to add (e.g., “Supplier”, “Product”) and the fields you need.**  \n2. **Do you already have or need a database migration script?**  \n3. **Any specific business rules (unique codes, status flags, soft‑delete) that should be enforced?**\n\nOnce I have those details, I can generate the precise PHP files and any helper code you’ll need.','2026-10-15 14:40:21'),
